ent": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "All three regions are on v2.3.0 and healthy, with error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002. Next I'm opening the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XahYaYscY6e1y5EHWcRezn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 has no healthy production history. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 is older). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial failure, leaving the fleet mixed: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt to v2.3.0 completed in all three regions. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west, eu-west; healthy=true; error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback; v2.3.1 must not be redeployed without change-manager approval since it has never been healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'm checking the incident list before retrying, to avoid paging on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0115AUZqDSdTy4yr9pnpVPnk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again. Error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 had no healthy production history, so I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy. No change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the fleet mixed. I retried once, and that attempt completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** The SEV2 incident creation timed out, but the incident was recorded as INC-0001. I checked the list and did not create a duplicate. The summary covers the rollback, the partial failure, and the follow-ups.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed without change-manager approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}